    "name_raw": "Deliberate Death",
    "definition_type_raw": "Origin",
    "source_book_raw": "Plane-Hopper's Handbook pg. 16",
    "definition_raw": "Source Plane-Hopper's Handbook pg. 16\nSomeone killed you: a monster, a murderer, a soldier, an executioner, it doesn’t matter—someone made a conscious decision to end your life.\n\nPrerequisites: Duskwalker.\n\nBenefit: Once per day, if you are reduced below 0 hit points as a result of an attack or ability used by another character, as an immediate action you can take a single standard action. You must use this action to attack or harm the creature that damaged you. At 11th level, you can use this feat a second time per day.",
    "links_raw": [
      {
        "anchor_text_raw": "Plane-Hopper's Handbook pg. 16",
        "href_raw": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy9z15?Pathfinder-Player-Companion-PlaneHopper-s-Handbook\n",
        "href_resolved": "http://paizo.com/products/btpy9z15?Pathfinder-Player-Companion-PlaneHopper-s-Handbook",
